#: 147e1c15a6804a03917ffbd1ceb4752a
msgid "Diátaxis as a guide to work"
msgstr ""

#: 446a2eb6f0c0486998ae966ae2c244ec
msgid "As well as providing a guide to documentation content, Diátaxis is also a guide to documentation process and execution."
msgstr ""

#: a0798ec2a4ab481786401ff8e3ab4374
msgid "Most people who work on technical documentation must make decisions about how to work, as they work. In some contexts, documentation must be delivered once, complete and in its final state, but it's more usual that it's an on-going project, for example developed alongside a product that itself evolves and develops. It's also the experience of many people who work on documentation to find themselves responsible for improving or even remediating a body of work."
msgstr ""

#: 71f4376c392045cfa83d2b981225197d
msgid "Diátaxis provides an approach to work that runs counter to much of the accepted wisdom in documentation. In particular, it discourages planning and top-down workflows, preferring instead small, responsive iterations from which overall patterns emerge."
msgstr ""

#: 6130843b67ba4ecfb430ff0892c5bf6a
msgid "Use Diátaxis as a guide, not a plan"
msgstr ""

#: ac232780ef65476183394030dd0dfefe
msgid "Diátaxis describes a complete picture of documentation. However the structure it proposes is not intended to be a **plan**, something you must complete in your documentation. It's a **guide**, a map to help you check that you're in the right place and going in the right directions."
msgstr ""

#: a639d9793b4640dfbf053090bf1ee41f
msgid "The point of Diátaxis is to give you a way to think about and understand your documentation, so that you can make better sense of what it's doing and what you're trying to do with it. It provides tools that help assess it, identify where its problems lie, and judge what you can do to improve it."
msgstr ""

#: 7f82ee6306f840d3ad2e046172e13482
msgid "Don't worry about structure"
msgstr ""

#: 16804cd1b6114a97880cdd4c0a53211f
msgid "Although structure is key to documentation, **using Diátaxis means not spending energy trying to get its structure correct**."
msgstr ""

#: 5da94365af7a473a87223bdfbeeeff7d
msgid "If you continue to follow the prompts that Diátaxis provides, eventually your documentation will assume the Diátaxis structure - but it will have assumed that shape *because* it has been improved. It's not the other way round, that the structure must be imposed upon documentation to improve it."
msgstr ""

#: b075af216dcf4cd485d76efa6076635d
msgid "Getting started with Diátaxis does not require you to think about dividing up your documentation into four sections. **It certainly does not mean that you should create empty structures for tutorials/howto guides/reference/explanation with nothing in them.** Don't do that. It's horrible."
msgstr ""

#: 083ded1ea9854d44bd5cfade51c8c2c1
msgid "Instead, following the workflow described in the next two sections, make changes where you see opportunities for improvement according to Diátaxis principles, so that the documentation starts to take a certain shape. At a certain point, the changes you have made will appear to demand that you move material under a certain Diátaxis heading - and that is how your top-level structure will form. In other words, **Diátaxis changes the structure of your documentation from the inside**."
msgstr ""

#: 28a911f4fc9747a6888c038946c5140b
msgid "Work one step at a time"
msgstr ""

#: ec13820f9c824d71a935db12629d96a4
msgid "Diátaxis strongly prescribes a structure, but whatever the state of your existing documentation - even if it's a complete mess by any standards - it's always possible to improve it, **iteratively**."
msgstr ""

#: f8773d0ce2cb4381a153fee5ec6bd358
msgid "It's natural to want to complete large tranches of work before you publish them, so that you have something substantial to show each time. Avoid this temptation - every step in the right direction is worth publishing immediately."
msgstr ""

#: fd851d3b3de64f0eaded5fd1ba32b99f
msgid "Although Diátaxis is intended to provide a big picture of documentation, **don't try to work on the big picture**. It's both unnecessary and unhelpful. Diátaxis is designed to guide small steps; keep taking small steps to arrive where you want to go."
msgstr ""

#: d47ff0bca5634550937dab4afe806a1f
msgid "Just do something"
msgstr ""

#: 61eaf98c0a034a7dbc0a9094eda3e6e1
msgid "If you're tidying up a huge mess, the temptation is to tear it all down and start again. Again, avoid it. As far as improving documentation in-line with Diátaxis goes, it isn't necessary to seek out things to improve. Instead, the best way to apply Diátaxis is as follows:"
msgstr ""

#: 3a018387a2ae46599a3e8c93ef0720e4
msgid "**Choose something** - any piece of the documentation. If you don’t already have something that you know you want to put right, don't go looking for outstanding problems. Just look at what you have right in front of you at that moment: the file you’re in, the last page you read - it doesn’t matter. If there isn’t one just choose something, literally at random."
msgstr ""

#: 1fcaab0ada154cc0aa001e7b5a19b8f0
msgid "**Assess it**. Next consider this thing critically. Preferably it’s a small thing, nothing bigger than a page - or better, even smaller, a paragraph or a sentence. Challenge it, according to the standards Diátaxis prescribes: *What user need is represented by this? How well does it serve that need? What can be added, moved, removed or changed to serve that need better? Do its language and logic meet the requirements of this mode of documentation?*"
msgstr ""

#: 589dcbeae94a433db137e6d9ee53c88d
msgid "**Decide what to do**. Decide, based on your answers to those questions: *What single next action will produce an immediate improvement here?*"
msgstr ""

#: 363be711d2e247358658bbfd4e2c606f
msgid "**Do it**. Complete that next single action, *and consider it completed* - i.e. publish it, or at least commit the change. Don't feel that you need to do anything else to make a worthy improvement."
msgstr ""

#: a8e7bf40418e476cb43368d0469adb7a
msgid "And then go back to the beginning of the cycle."
msgstr ""

#: 61837c0420be4cb7863a9c1d142cebfa
msgid "Working like this helps reduce the stress of one of the most paralysing and troublesome aspects of the documentation-writer's work: working out what to do. It keeps work flowing in the right direction, always towards the desired end, without having to expend energies on a plan."
msgstr ""

#: 7ebeae5ec85b401684065f5d0d56a6cf
msgid "Allow your work to develop organically"
msgstr ""

#: dd2fb585abfc4467bce032c3e5c48e25
msgid "There's a strong urge to work in a cycle of planning and execution in order to work towards results. But it's not the only way, and there are often better ways when working with documentation."
msgstr ""

#: 8ca8b3b62b1049369dc67307dd719be7
msgid "Well-formed organic growth"
msgstr ""

#: e18261e5c18a48b3b74aca465bf76c3b
msgid "A good model for documentation is **well-formed organic growth that adapts to external conditions**. Organic growth takes place at the cellular level. The structure of the organism as a whole is guaranteed by the healthy development of cells, according to rules that are appropriate to each kind of cell. It's not the other way round, that a structure is imposed on the organism from above or outside. Good structure develops from within."
msgstr ""

#: d419eaa43b834ee1abf91f9b8f677668
msgid "Illustration copyright `Linette Voller <https://linettevoller.com>`_ 2021, reproduced with kind permission."
msgstr ""

#: b7d3f68fa5e1431399e14c2a4ab69d91
msgid "It's the same with documentation: by following the principles that Diátaxis provides, your documentation will attain a healthy structure, because its internal components themselves are well-formed - like a living organism, it will have built itself up from the inside-out, one cell at a time."
msgstr ""

#: b62a761bd59d4e19b320ec7e0e761b72
msgid "Complete, not finished"
msgstr ""

#: 3d57a696346645059944f70f5f045f90
msgid "Consider a plant. As a living, growing organism, a plant is **never finished** - it can always develop further, move on to the next stage of growth and maturity. But, at every stage of its development, from seed to a fully-mature tree, it's **always complete** - there's never something missing from it. At any point, it is in a state that is appropriate to its stage of development."
msgstr ""

#: fe8eea45cdda497a88abb3e4f78d0f34
msgid "Similarly, documentation is also never finished, because it always has to keep adapting and changing to the product and to users' needs, and can always be developed and improved further."
msgstr ""

#: bb6d36d75e3c424d99ec27681fa7be01
msgid "However it can always be complete: useful to users, appropriate to its current stage of development, and in a healthy structural state and ready to go on to the next stage."
msgstr ""
